            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <button class="faq-q">How long does it take to lower body fat percentage? <span>+</span></button>
                <div class="faq-a"><p>A safe and sustainable rate is losing about 0.5–1% body fat per month through a moderate calorie deficit, strength training, and adequate protein. Faster loss usually means losing muscle along with fat.</p></div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <button class="faq-q">Why do women have higher body fat than men? <span>+</span></button>
                <div class="faq-a"><p>Women need more essential fat for hormonal balance, reproductive function, and overall health. A woman at 25% body fat can be just as fit and healthy as a man at 15% — the ranges are different by design, not by lack of fitness.</p></div>
            </div>

